                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 1,
                    "title": "Aim",
                    "new_page": false,
                    "text": "To design and study a lithography mask pattern for shallow trench isolation, illustrating line space structures within a defined boundary for device isolation for given masks."
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 2,
                    "title": "Tool",
                    "new_page": false,
                    "text": "Semulator3D"
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 3,
                    "title": "THEORY",
                    "new_page": false,
                    "text": [
                        "Shallow Trench Isolation (STI) is a semiconductor fabrication technique used to electrically isolate adjacent devices. In this process, shallow trenches are formed in the silicon substrate and filled with an insulating material. Lithography is used to define the regions where the trenches are to be formed.",
                        "In this assignment, two lithography mask designs are studied. Design 1 consists of a 500 nm \u00d7 400 nm boundary containing four vertical mask openings, each 40 nm wide and separated by 60 nm spacing. The openings form a regular line-space grating oriented along the Y-axis. Design 2 consists of a 500 nm \u00d7 500 nm boundary with a 60 nm wide horizontal bar and a 60 nm wide vertical bar, both extending across the complete boundary and intersecting at the center.",
                        "These patterns illustrate how lithographic dimensions such as opening width, spacing, orientation, and alignment are used to define regions for device isolation. Precise control of these parameters is important for transferring the required pattern accurately during semiconductor fabrication."
                    ]
                },
