                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 7,
                    "title": "Observation",
                    "new_page": false,
                    "text": [
                        "Design 1 showed four uniform vertical line openings within the 500 nm \u00d7 400 nm boundary. Each line was 40 nm wide with 60 nm spacing, producing a regular line-space grating along the Y-axis.",
                        "Design 2 showed a cross-shaped pattern within the 500 nm \u00d7 500 nm boundary. The horizontal and vertical openings were each 60 nm wide, extended across the full boundary, and intersected at the center."
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "type": "text",
                    "number": 8,
                    "title": "Conclusion",
                    "new_page": false,
                    "text": "The lithography mask patterns for shallow trench isolation were successfully designed and studied using Semulator3D. The parallel line array and orthogonal cross pattern were created with the specified dimensions, spacing, orientation, and boundary limits. The experiment demonstrated how accurately defined mask openings are used to represent isolation regions during semiconductor fabrication."
